\cf4 Nabu\'92s loss of innocence came from growing up reading mythology, fairytales, and Goosebumps books, lamenting that magic didn\'92t exist anymore and that history was over, with everything having been discovered or explained. It was during this time that they started to realize the opposite\'97that magic still existed and that there was more to discover and explore, which allowed them to regain their innocence and embrace a renewed sense of wonder. This shift became a pivotal moment in their spiritual and creative journey. Nabu views the loss of innocence as the loss of joy and wonder, often linked to the systemic suppression of these qualities, particularly through societal attitudes toward sexuality. They see this as a common cause of the loss of joy and wonder in many people's lives. This perspective has shaped their understanding of how external systems impact individual growth, creativity, and spiritual awakening.\nestcell 
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\sl280\partightenfactor0
