\cf4 Nabu believes that reclaiming joy and wonder is deeply connected to laughter. They view laughter as a central part of their creative expression and spiritual practices, as it allows them to reconnect with innocence and navigate the complexities of life with levity. Humor serves as both a tool for healing and a way to challenge societal norms, bringing lightness to deep themes and creating space for growth and transformation. However, Nabu recognizes laughter as an unconscious defense mechanism they wish they didn't rely on. While it serves as a way to cope with difficult emotions and situations, they also acknowledge that it can sometimes mask deeper feelings or complexities they would prefer to confront directly. Despite its usefulness, they view this reliance on humor as something they would like to move beyond.\nestcell 
